5. Cross-Domain Intelligence (Capacity + Resilience)
High-value combined insights captured in the notes:

• Over-utilized + weak timeout/retry strategy -> scaling alone will not stabilize the service.
• Under-utilized but low resilience coverage -> cost-optimized but operationally fragile.
• Capacity spikes explained by downstream failure plus retry amplification -> fix dependency behavior first, then right-size.
• Recurrent incidents where resilience tests fail the same pattern -> mandatory governance gate before release.
6. Production Requirements
6.1 Robustness
• Idempotent ingestion and replay support.
• Partial-source failure tolerance with degraded-confidence output.
• Strong audit trail for each playbook step and decision.
• RBAC plus approval gates for disruptive tests.
6.2 Efficiency
• Incremental data pulls using watermark-based extraction.
• Pre-aggregated time windows for CPU and latency statistics.
• Caching of topology and static capability scans.
• Asynchronous playbook execution with prioritized queues.
6.3 Scalability
• Horizontal scaling for connectors and playbook workers.
• Partitioning by app/service/environment.
• High-volume metrics stored in time-series storage, with findings in relational/document stores.
• Event-driven trigger model for near-real-time anomaly handling.
